LIMITS = [
 ("h2", "Limitations and reproducibility"),
 ("p", "Three limits bound what the comparison can support. The grid is finite: k is enumerated up to a stated maximum, the maximum differs by rule, and a design outside it is not covered; where the last admissible k sits at the grid edge we report the smallest known admissible k instead of a verdict of infeasibility, and 437 of the 660 groups in the feasible-set experiment reach that edge. The admissible set is defined by three service rates at a tolerance, so the paper describes configurations that meet a standard and does not prove that one of them is socially preferable: cost items whose parameters are not identified for the site, namely the value of time, the search and detour durations [[34-36]], the externality factors, the relocation cost and the charging-want share, keep the social total not computable, and no configuration is called a social optimum anywhere in this paper. Finally, the trajectories are two days of one city: the demand model does not contain decision-dependent arrivals, so a lot that becomes easier to park in is not allowed to become more attractive, and the counterfactual demand under a different rule is an assumption rather than an estimate."),
 ("p", "Each experiment carries its own boundary. The mechanism traces are synthetic configurations of the mechanism model replayed in the event simulator; they explain an observed non-monotonicity and they are not measurements of a real lot, so they cannot be read as evidence that a particular site behaves this way. The information experiment compares two implemented policies, an exact reproduction of the real rule and a heuristic available only in an analysis-only regime, and it therefore bounds neither the value of the information nor the performance of the best policy. The feasible-set experiment enumerates a grid and takes the service rates at one tolerance; the empty sets it reports are empty inside the grid, and the sets it reports as truncated may or may not contain admissible counts beyond it. None of the three replaces a deployment study."),
 ("p", "The literature enters with its own evidence levels, and they are not uniform. The shared allocation papers are cited for their model structure. The joint-operation model is cited for its decision variables, information structure and objective form, and its propositions are not quoted because the appendix containing the proofs was not obtained. The charging-use ratios are observed frequencies from another country and another decade, and one of the two source tables is a provisional transcription. None of these is used to calibrate a parameter of the site studied here, and a reader should not take them as such."),
 ("p", "The monotonicity result is a proposition for a restricted no-fallback variant under six stated assumptions, with the proof in Supplementary Note S2: it is not a theorem about parking systems, the enumeration is a supporting check, and its failure set is nested in the direction opposite to the decrease that motivates the question. The two smaller counts in the rule comparison are two pairwise comparisons on a single lot-seed group and not two independent groups, every interval statement holds within the enumerated range 0-40, and the 437 truncated sets are unknown beyond that range rather than inadmissible. Supplementary Notes S1-S6 accompany this paper as a separate file and carry the conventions, the proof, the trajectory and control tables, the per-unit comparison, the full rule-pair table and the audit record."),
 ("p", "Every number reported above comes from a command recorded with its interpreter, exit code, input hashes and frozen versions; the commands, the interpreter versions, the input hashes and the render checks are listed in Supplementary Note S6 rather than repeated here. The static planning problem is checked in a second implementation and agrees to floating-point tolerance (441 rows compared, maximum absolute difference 4.5e-12, all 145 checks passed), while the event-driven simulation itself has not been duplicated in that second implementation, so the reproduction claim is limited to what was actually re-run. Results computed under an earlier accounting keep their version label and are not recomputed by relabelling, and any item that could not be verified is listed with the unverified items rather than dropped from the text."),

]


